From aae88321e546d0a9058fd49f3c6446b762bf41be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 04:07:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Solvers and preconditioners of Trilinos

Module of the factories of linear solvers and preconditioners for
Trilinos (option enable-trilinos, Trilinos found by find_package with
Tpetra, Belos, Amesos2, Ifpack2, MueLu and ShyLU_DDFROSch):

- BelosSolver: the Krylov solvers of Belos (CG, GMRES, ...), with a
  preconditioner of Trilinos, which shares the matrix of the solver, or of
  mfem-mgis, applied to vectors of MFEM;
- Amesos2Solver and Amesos2Preconditioner: the direct solvers of Amesos2
  (KLU2, Tacho if available, ...);
- Ifpack2 (relaxations, Chebyshev polynomial, incomplete factorizations),
  MueLu (smoothed aggregation multigrid, with the rigid body modes, the
  number of components and the coordinates of the nodes, deterministic
  aggregates and silent setup by default) and FROSch (two level
  overlapping Schwarz preconditioner, additive, with the null space of the
  linear elasticity) as preconditioners.

The sources including Trilinos are compiled by the compiler of Kokkos in
a shared library (MFEMMGISTrilinos) whose interface only uses standard
types (TrilinosBackend.hxx). The unknowns ordered by nodes are permuted,
process by process, to be ordered by vector dimension. When MFEM and
Tpetra compute on a GPU, the vectors are copied on the GPU; Kokkos is
initialized on demand by mfem-mgis. The rows of the Dirichlet boundary
conditions are not given to FROSch: the list built by
FindOneEntryOnlyRowsGlobal made its initialization hang on several
processes with three unknowns per node (FROSch 17.2.1).
